WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.390
Good morning, John!

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:07.160
Most of you, 99%, aren't gonna be able to
be at VidCon and, so, you don't wanna hear

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.880
about how great it's gonna be.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.809
So, in lieu of being at VidCon or either if
you are gonna be there, I'm gonna give you

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:14.809
an assignment.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:17.050
VidCon is all about celebrating and appreciating
the culture of online video.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.909
But as, John, you so wisely pointed out last
video, we're pretty old.

00:00:21.909 --> 00:00:25.689
The first time I got obsessed with a video
that I downloaded from the internet was 1998.

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:30.060
The year before that was when the very first
viral internet video happened - uh, it was

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.640
just this dancing baby.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.820
Except you gotta go "UGACHACA UGAUGAUGACHACA
UGAUGAUGA" (keeps chanting that while singing)

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:41.100
I can't stop this feelin', deep inside of
me."

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:49.090
In fact, I have been into online video for
longer than some of you have been in the world.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.100
Which makes me...kinda depressed.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:56.530
But it also might actually make me that elusive
thing - an expert.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.490
So, here's what we're gonna do.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:03.200
You're gonna listen to me talk about how great
the old days were and then you're gonna indulge

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.920
me by going to watch a bunch of old online
video that I think is better than anything

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.130
being created today, despite mountains of
evidence to the contrary.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.270
It's just like any other course you've ever
taken.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.990
The dancing baby is not in the category of
things that I think are really fantastic and

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:17.990
great.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:23.399
But a couple years later, in the year 2000,
a project was launched that became the best,

00:01:23.399 --> 00:01:27.979
and remains the best, online video project
in history.

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:33.249
Homestar Runner is some kind of bizarre, alien
thing that lives in Free Country, USA, with

00:01:33.249 --> 00:01:38.390
his friends: his girlfriend, Marzipan, who's
a baseball bat with hair in a dress; Coach

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:44.009
Z and Pom-Pom and the Cheat and King of Town
and Strong Mad, who is just a square, and

00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:51.109
Strong Sad, who is sad and circular and Strong
Bad, who, despite having boxing gloves for

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:53.899
hands, types out responses to e-mails every
week.

00:01:53.899 --> 00:01:56.999
There's so much good Homestar Runner content!

00:01:56.999 --> 00:02:03.630
You need to grab a friend and take them and
take this wonderful thing that exists into

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.630
your life!

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.630
It's really good.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:06.630
HomestarRunner.com.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:07.630
Check it out.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:12.750
And note that when we started watching that
show, that little thing took up our entire

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:13.860
computer monitors!

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.250
And then weep for us.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:18.430
There's a kid just fell off a bike outside
of my window.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.430
He's okay.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.430
He's fine.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.430
At the same time as Homestar Runner, there
was all kinds of really interesting Flash

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:25.240
animation stuff happening: The End of the
World, All Your Base Are Belong To Us, Peanut

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:30.090
Butter Jelly Time - these are things that
are important pieces of the culture of the

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.090
Internet.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.270
We also got what was probably the first Internet
native genre of video, the animutation.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.310
The animutations were brought into the world
by a lot of different people, but they were

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:42.310
pioneered by a guy who you might know from
his later work, "The Mysterious Ticking Noise,"

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:43.320
Neil Cicierega.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.840
But when bandwidth got good enough, people
could actually start to send and receive video.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.840
THIS kind of video.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:54.160
And the most important video series of all
time was, of course, "The Show with Ze Frank."

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.610
The show revolutionized video.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.970
It took advantage of the fact that the Internet
is a two-way medium.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.570
It allowed people to participate in the project.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.350
It wasn't just about Ze; it was about the
entire sportsracer community.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.650
Pretty much anything you watch on YouTube
nowadays is either directly or indirectly

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:09.870
influenced by Ze Frank.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:14.260
All this stuff was extremely important in
the Internet's ability to establish itself

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:19.250
as its own, stand-alone legitimate culture,
and since YouTube came along, yes, many more

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.370
amazing things have happened.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:25.160
So much amazing stuff is being made now that
of course, I can't even start to talk about

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.680
what's happened since YouTube existed.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.900
This is almost a kind of pre-history of Internet
video that I'm talking about right now, and

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:36.050
I think that it's important for us to understand
that stuff, for us to know where it all came

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.050
from.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:42.700
Also, it's just amazingly fun to enjoy, so
grab a friend, click the links in the description

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.750
and just enjoy.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.820
Now I have to go back to VidCon stuff.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.320
I want this video to keep going!

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.140
I want to keep making this video!

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.680
I don't wanna work on VidCon.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.660
Okay, I'm gonna do it, though.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:54.760
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

